#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# collect

#% text
# `collect(e, x)` expands e and gathers its terms by powers of x, with the coefficient of each power in front.

#% text
# `collect(e, x, h)` applies h to each coefficient; `collect(e, [x1, x2, ...])` collects in x1, then the coefficients in x2, and so on.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Powers may be rational or symbolic. Lists are handled element-wise.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
collect(b*x^2 + 5*x + 7*x^2 + 9*a*x + 2, x)
#% output
#= 2 + x*(5 + 9*a) + (7 + b)*x^2

#% cell
collect((1 + a + x)^3, x)
#% output
#= 1 + 3*a + 3*a^2 + x*(3 + 6*a + 3*a^2) + (3 + 3*a)*x^2 + a^3 + x^3

#% cell
collect((1 + a + x)^3, x, factor)
#% output
#= 3*x*(1 + a)^2 + 3*(1 + a)*x^2 + x^3 + (1 + a)^3

#% cell
collect(a*sqrt(x) + sqrt(x) + 3*x - c*x + 5, x)
#% output
#= 5 + x*(3 - c) + (1 + a)*x^(1/2)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `expand`, `coefficient`, `exponent`, `factor_terms`
